Stage: MD

Purpose:
  Mobile stage. Owns the mobile implementation of the unit of work — UI,
  client-side state, integration against the API contract — everything
  QA needs already working before it can validate the feature
  end-to-end on mobile.


Requires:
  API (see stages/API.sdd -> Blocks)


Produces:
  Working mobile implementation, integrated against the API contract,
  ready for QA.


Blocks:
  QA — QA MUST NOT validate a stage that has not executed (see
  chains.sdd -> Rules [C5]).


Parallel:
  MAY execute in parallel with FE when both depend only on API and are
  otherwise independent of each other (see chains.sdd ->
  ParallelExample).


Optional:
  Skipped (never silently — see chains.sdd -> Rules [C7]) when the unit
  of work does not affect mobile — this is the exact condition
  chains.sdd -> MobileExample illustrates.


Skills:
  @../../skills/mobile/

  (see chains.sdd -> DoesNotOwn — this file defines WHEN/responsibility
  only; HOW the mobile change is actually implemented belongs to
  skills/mobile/, not here.)


State: + (vocabulary defined here; skills/mobile/ content is not yet
  written — see skills/skills.sdd -> SkillDomains, state: boş)


Note:
  (prompt/new/33.md, STEP 11) Extracted out of the flat feature.chain /
  bugfix.chain / change.chain, where the MD responsibility was repeated
  inline in each file. Defined once here per NoDuplication; referenced
  from chains.sdd -> Stages and from every template under ./templates/
  that includes an MD step.
